{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And His anger burned.</b> Rabbi Yehoshua ben Korchah says: every instance of burning anger in Scripture leaves a mark, but this one — no mark was stated in it, nor do we find any punishment came through that burning. Rabbi Yosei said to him: even in this one a mark is stated in it — <b>Is not Aharon your brother the Levite</b> — that he was destined to be a Levite and not a priest; and the priesthood, I would have said, was to come forth from you; from now on it shall not be so, but he shall be priest and you the Levite, as it is said: ״וּמֹשֶׁה אִישׁ הָאֱלֹהִים בָּנָיו יִקָּרְאוּ עַל שֵׁבֶט הַלֵּוִי״ (I Chronicles 23) (Zevachim 102)." "<b>Behold, he is going out to meet you.</b> When you go to Egypt." "<b>And when he sees you he will rejoice in his heart.</b> Not as you suppose — that he would resent you for rising to greatness. From this Aharon merited the breastplate of decision set upon the heart (Shabbat 139)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {2 "Cited as Shabbat 139a; the reference is to the Urim vetummim on the high priest's breastplate."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:33.327445575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}